nd our nation’s security. I encourage all news stations to broadcast this deliberately nonpartisan speech." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 5371, "fields": { "question": 1105, "description": "We might need to spend some time shoring up party unity in the Conservative party, lest a faction of the party’s turnout ends up being depressed. We need all hands on deck to win this election with a functional majority." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 5372, "fields": { "question": 1106, "description": "I am happy with our progress thus far at appealing to 2016 Leave voters, and it will continue. We will withdraw from the European Union in my next term and that’s final. Brexit means Brexit." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 5373, "fields": { "question": 1106, "description": "I won’t directly try to appeal to UKIP voters, as that might turn off other voters. However I will stress my policies for reducing immigration, including an Australian-style points based system, that will keep out low skilled migrants who will lower British wages." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 5374, "fields": { "question": 1106, "description": "Brexit means Brexit, and if we can’t get a deal that respects our strong red lines in regards to immigration, then we’re willing to leave without a deal altogether. No deal is better than a bad deal." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 5375, "fields": { "question": 1106, "description": "Appealing to 2015 UKIP voters is too risky. We need to primarily focus on Labour voters if we’re going to increase our majority like I set out to. Also we can’t alienate our Blue Wall. We can’t have an exodus of voters in the South or in Scotland." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 5376, "fields": { "question": 1107, "description": "If we’re going to beat back this hard right protest party, we have to take strong stances that appeal to them. We will promise that the UK will fully leave the EU by the end of 2018 and we will have net-zero immigration." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 5377, "fields": { "question": 1107, "description": "Immigration is a very important issue to these voters, so I will lean on my credentials as the architect of the Hostile Environment policy that has seen over 100,000 illegal immigrants voluntarily leave our country." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 5378, "fields": { "question": 1107, "description": "Oh, that is worrying. We are the party that gave the Brexit referendum, there’s a problem if they’re not backing us. We need to make a strong stance and do it now. No deal is better than a bad deal. If I can’t get a deal that respects British sovereignty, I will leave without a deal." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 5379, "fields": { "question": 1107, "description": "We have to be very careful. We must do something to prevent UKIP dividing the Conservative vote, but we can’t alienate Southern and Scottish remain voters. Oh dear, this is a difficult balancing act. We will continue our current campaign and hope we can attract UKIP votes." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 5380, "fields": { "question": 1108, "description": "We have no need to expend too much campaign energy here. Our campaign is clearly effective at appealing to these voters how it is, so we do not need to change anything on this front." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 5381, "fields": { "question": 1108, "description": "There is no need to do so, we’re already successful with these voters, so let’s instead campaign harder with Leave voters. We will win this election with a strong majority if we’re able to balance our appeal between Remainers and Leavers." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer", "pk": 5382, "fields": { "question": 1108, "description": "I will. My promise is that I will get a Brexit deal for the country that does not break us off from Europe. If you support remaining in the European E