ry strong stance with its support to Thatcher’s reforms, and believes that these should be returned to. This includes massive tax cuts to businesses, broad privatisation of social services aside for the NHS, and restrictions on trade union activity that can interfere with the free market.", "election": 20 } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.issue", "pk": 102, "fields": { "name": "National Security", "description": "In an increasingly dangerous world, people are asking what is needed to keep Britain safe. Others are concerned that these ideas threaten their rights to privacy. National security is a contentious issue after the occurrence of multiple deadly terror attacks in Europe recently.", "stance_1": "Strongly Privacy", "stance_desc_1": "The seat has extremely strong concerns about increasing governmental powers to interfere in their lives over issues of national security. With the exposure of mass surveillance from the GCHQ in 2013, these fears were realised to be happening, and there are great fears that such surveillance will be escalated against their wishes.", "stance_2": "Privacy", "stance_desc_2": "The seat has strong concerns about increasing governmental powers to surveil their lives over national security concerns. With the exposure of mass surveillance from the GCHQ in 2013, these fears would be realised. As such, many constituents in this seat are concerned about infringements on their right to privacy.", "stance_3": "Lean Privacy", "stance_desc_3": "The seat has concerns about increasing governmental powers to surveil their lives over national security concerns. However, there is an understanding that policy is needed to make Britain safer. As such whilst they have concerns about overreach, there are some compromises they will accept to accomplish this.", "stance_4": "Neutral", "stance_desc_4": "The seat takes a moderate stance in regards to national security, both having equal concerns about their rights being infringed upon, and concerns about their personal safety being in danger from external threats. As such, they support some national security legislation to be implemented, but are concerned about overreach", "stance_5": "Lean Security", "stance_desc_5": "The seat has concerns about increasing danger in the world and at home, and believe something has to be done to protect the lives of British citizens, however in the backs of their minds, the average constituent of this seat has in mind some concerns about governmental overreach.", "stance_6": "Security", "stance_desc_6": "The seat has serious concerns about Britain getting more dangerous and believes something has to be done to protect the lives of British citizens, even if this involves some rights being curtailed in the process. Something has to be done.", "stance_7": "Strongly Security", "stance_desc_7": "The seat has extremely serious concerns about growing threats both internal and external in the UK, and as such, supports broad overwhelming reforms to stamp out the threat of terrorism. Even if this affects personal rights, the average constituent in this seat believes it’s justified to make the country safer.", "election": 20 } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.issue", "pk": 103, "fields": { "name": "Social", "description": "The stance the seat takes on social issues. Progressive seats are more likely to support rights for women, ethnic minorities and LGBT+ people, whilst conservative seats are more likely to support traditional marriage, tough on crime policies, and support British traditions like grammar schools and fox hunting.", "stance_1": "Very Progressive", "stance_desc_1": "The seat is very in support of broad social justice policies, protecting the rights for gender equality, racial equality, support for transgender rights, among other issues. The constituents of these seats tend to be young, urban, educated, and passionately vocal in these beliefs.", "stance_2": "Progressive", "stance_desc_2": "The seet is in support of social justice reforms, closing the gender pay gap, greater protections for ethnic minorities and LGBT+ people. The constituents are likely young, mostly urban, and educated, although their vote might not as strongly be drawn based on these issues.", "stance_3": "Lean Progressive", "stance_desc_3": "The seat leans towards being in support of social equality, such as supporting the closure of the gender pay gap and further protections for ethnic minorities as well as some protections for LGBT+ people, but isn’t too strongly invested in these issues. Some constituents may have concerns about the speed of progress.", "stance_4": "Moderate", "stance_desc_4": "The seat doesn’t take a strong side on social issues, or is made up by populations that are both progressive and conservative. The average constituent of these seats generally isn’t paying attention to social issues, and may tacitly support some social reforms, but generally other issues are on their minds.", "stance_5": "Lean Conservative", "stance_desc_5": "The seat leans towards supporting British tradition, scepticism of recent social progress, and is likely supportive of tough-on-crime policies. Many constituents support harsher sentencing for criminals, although are not supportive of controversial traditions like fox hunting. The average voter in the seat is likely older than the national average.", "stance_6": "Conservative", "stance_desc_6": "The seat generally supports British tradition, tough on crime policies, and is opposed to recent social progress. This may indicate a general feeling of opposition to same-sex marriage for the average constituent, or it may represent a more passionate support of British traditions.", "stance_7": "Very Conservative", "stance_desc_7": "The seat either is very passionate for preserving and reviving British traditions or holds very conservative views in response to social issues and criminal justice, many supporting reviving the death penalty for serious crimes. Seats in this category tend to be ve