ck": "Brexit will likely be your strongest issue, so beginning your quest to achieve a strong majority may benefit from placing the issue of the UK's relation to Europe front and centre." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2501, "fields": { "answer": 5002, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "With this being the first election post-Brexit, the Conservatives haven’t had such a great opportunity to evolve their appeal. In this election, working class people have the potential to vote Tory in numbers never seen before." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2502, "fields": { "answer": 5003, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Polls are showing a slight weakening of the SNP compared to their 2015 landslide. Ruth Davidson must be commemorated for her work at presenting the Conservatives as the primary unionist opposition to the Scottish Nationals." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2503, "fields": { "answer": 5004, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "An election campaign in a time like this needs a strong pitch that both appeals wide and deep. This message hits the spot. " } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2504, "fields": { "answer": 5005, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "You haven’t given a policy reason to justify voting Conservative, but maybe the idea here is you don’t actually need one. Your opponent will just drive concerned moderates into the Tory column." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2513, "fields": { "answer": 5006, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "It’s a tried-and-true strategy. When your opponent neglects the centre, you swoop in and capitalise on the opportunity. However, in an environment of growing Conservative factionalism, this move risks alienating some of the hard-right members of the party." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2514, "fields": { "answer": 5007, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "We’re unsure about this being a good approach. The Conservatives strongest appeal at the moment comes from Brexit. You might be playing into Labour’s strengths here. " } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2515, "fields": { "answer": 5008, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": " A solid performance for us in the local elections. We gained a net 536 councillors as well as having a surprising upset victory in the Tees Valley mayoral race with Ben Houchen beating Sue Jeffrey by 0.2%." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2516, "fields": { "answer": 5009, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Surprisingly, we managed to win in both of these mayoral races. Ben Houchen won by 0.4% and Andy Street by 1.1%. Alongside that we gained a respectable 498 councillors." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2517, "fields": { "answer": 5010, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Despite the overall focus being moved towards the general election, you can’t complain at 453 new Tory councillors entering into councils around the country. Andy Street barely lost the West Midlands mayoral race by 0.2%." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2518, "fields": { "answer": 5011, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "You net a respectable 504 councillors in total, many across Scotland with Andy Street narrowly winning the West Midlands mayoral race. You’ve got to be satisfied with that." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2519, "fields": { "answer": 5012, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "That might be your best option, but the more extreme factions of the Traditionalist wing push for fox hunting to be codified in the manifesto. Not wanting a walk-out of these MPs, you acquiesce." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2520, "fields": { "answer": 5013, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "The Traditionalists are happy to hear this, and they will more enthusiastically sing your praises. On the other hand, your vocal support of fox hunting will surely bring up inconvenient questions." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2521, "fields": { "answer": 5014, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "It’s difficult to know what to do in regards to this question. If you deny it, you alienate a very vocal group of MPs, if you accept it, you raise questions about animal cruelty. Perhaps you’re trying to have your cake and eat it too." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2522, "fields": { "answer": 5015, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Overall in an ideal situation, this would be the clear answer, but in a fractured Conservative party, you are for sure going to receive disdain for refusing to offer the vote." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2523, "fields": { "answer": 5016, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Okay Mrs Prime Minister, we have a title and an outline for the manifesto, how would you like to present the information?" } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2524, "fields": { "answer": 5017, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Okay Mrs Prime Minister, we have a title and an outline for the manifesto, how would you like to present the information?" } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2525, "fields": { "answer": 5019, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Okay Mrs Prime Minister, we have a title and an outline for the manifesto, how would you like to present the information?" } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2526, "fields": { "answer": 5020, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "It’s expected this manifesto will be a rather jack of all trades sort of manuscript. It’s unlikely it will reach far with any specific group, but may keep a wide array of different voter factions mildly contented." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2527, "fields": { "answer": 5021, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "It’s expected this manifesto will play alright with many different groups. It might help in the Red Wall with its simpler formatting." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2528, "fields": { "answer": 5022, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "It’s expected that this manifesto will play best in London and the Home Countries, where there are more educated voters." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2529, "fields": { "answer": 5023, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Okay, Our plan with this manifesto is that it will play best within two regions. It will be strong in London we believe, as well as possibly being strong in Scotland if you play your cards right." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2530, "fields": { "answer": 5024, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Hmm… Whilst this appeared like a good strategy at first, it seems voters are demanding more than just “not being Corbyn”. Let’s hope it doesn’t affect them turning out for the Conservatives." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2531, "fields": { "answer": 5025, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "You hurl a slew of attacks at your main opposition in this race. This is often unwise when you’re well ahead in the polls, but as the momentum is starting to pick up for your opponent, maybe breaking orthodoxy is a good idea here?" } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2532, "fields": { "answer": 5026, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "This is likely a good decision. Our current polls suggest that Brexit is our strongest issue." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2533, "fields": { "answer": 5027, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "With the terrorist attacks in France over the last couple of years, this might not be a bad idea. Many are concerned about their safety from similar attacks potentially happening at home." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2534, "fields": { "answer": 5028, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "You unveil your manifesto in Kilburn to a somewhat apathetic crowd of Londoners, ending without much fanfare or interest, which contrasts with Jeremy Corbyn’s much more explosive start out of the Labour manifesto unveiling." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2535, "fields": { "answer": 5029, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "To an audience of roughly 100, mostly made up by students and academics, you release a manifesto that got a few paying attention, a little bit of interest that paled in comparison to Corbyn’s manifesto unveiling." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2536, "fields": { "answer": 5031, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "You head up to Giffnock in East Renfrewshire and you deliver a rather uninspired unveiling of your manifesto. You ended up quickly taking a backseat to Ruth Davidson who managed to inspire a little enthusiasm for the Scottish Conservative cause, which contrasts with a very enthusiastic Corbyn manifesto unveiling." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2537, "fields": { "answer": 5000, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Alright, time to end Parliamentary gridlock, and this is a great message to start on in the face of such an unpopular opponent." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2538, "fields": { "answer": 5034, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "We’re not so sure. We don’t think this is something you can just dance around, it will come back to bite you in the debates." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2544, "fields": { "answer": 5033, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "We understand your need to get back campaigning again as soon as possible, so we’ll give some brief lessons to hopefully iron out the biggest flaws in your communication ability. " } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2545, "fields": { "answer": 5035, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "You will have a light schedule for the next week as we work to help you overcome these issues in your campaign." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2546, "fields": { "answer": 5036, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Of course this would come back to bite us, but giving a short gesture towards party unity and getting the conversation back to Brexit might be the best way you can handle it." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2547, "fields": { "answer": 5037, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Leaning into this very unpopular policy among the public will not help your campaign. At least Jacob Rees-Mogg is happy though." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2548, "fields": { "answer": 5040, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "It’s appreciated that you’re trying to reduce the temperature after such a shocking act of inhumanity." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2552, "fields": { "answer": 5041, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "As you visit Manchester, you end up meeting Jeremy Corbyn who is shaking hands with the family members of victims. You also meet up with them and connect on a personal level. The news broadcasts a heartwarming scene of both party leaders putting politics aside in the face of tragedy." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2553, "fields": { "answer": 5042, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Many nod along with these ideas, but they aren’t without controversy. Young people are concerned about the ideas of internet surveillance." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2554, "fields": { "answer": 5043, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "It’s difficult to consider what should be said after an attack like this to minimise future harm. A horrible attack is likely to result in a horrible backlash, and many British Muslims appreciate that you haven’t roped them into this, although UKIP call the Conservatives weak on terrorism, like clockwork." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2555, "fields": { "answer": 5044, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "You can’t say that austerity has failed publicly, but some subtle proposals to reverse some of the most severe cuts might play well in this political climate. Police funding is an area that even the most fiscal conservative partisans can’t attack without coming off as unreasonable." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2556, "fields": { "answer": 5045, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "What is national security but just another Brexit issue? Brexit, Brexit, Brexit. That’s your strength, so trying to wrestle control of the national conversation in this way might be a good approach." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2561, "fields": { "answer": 5046, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "It’s rich that Jeremy Corbyn is trying to hang the issue of national security over the heads of the Conservatives, but it’s frustrating that this is being rather successful against us. Perhaps reminding people of who Jeremy Corbyn is will get them to see sense once again?" } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2562, "fields": { "answer": 5047, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Bring it back to square 1. You’re already on the process to addressing these concerns. This election pivots on Brexit. In the end, who do you want leading the country into Donald Tusk’s negotiation room? Get the voters to think about that." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2563, "fields": { "answer": 5048, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "With the recent hype of the national security issue, making an argument for a Hard Brexit with the appearance of an argument about national security might make the Hard Brexit medicine go down better." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2564, "fields": { "answer": 5049, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "You are clarifying a preference for a Soft Brexit. This will help with moderates and Remain voters, it will likely be popular in Scotland, but you might struggle to pull UKIP’s votes towards the Conservatives if you make your Brexit stance too “soft”." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2568, "fields": { "answer": 5050, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "The “no-deal” option sends shivers down the spines of Remainers, many of which are looking to desert the Conservative ship any way they can, but this strength is perceived with much more positivity in the Red Wall." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2569, "fields": { "answer": 5051, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Ruling out the no-deal option pacifies many Remainers, but it’s not like you’ve given a Soft Brexit position here. This very much still expresses issues like border security. In essence, it’s as big a tent as you can make the Brexit issue. Many are content, but not many are enthusiastic." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2570, "fields": { "answer": 5052, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "That’s all they wanted to hear. “Brexit means Brexit”, music to the UKIP supporters’ ears." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2571, "fields": { "answer": 5053, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Many UKIP voters concern themselves heavily with immigration, and this idea of a “points-based” system has been picking up steam on the political right. This should win over a decent amount of UKIP’s support." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2572, "fields": { "answer": 5054, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Leaning in on the no-deal idea will certainly win over a lot of UKIP voters, but also it will alienate a lot of Remain voters from the Conservative camp. " } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2573, "fields": { "answer": 5055, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "The “UKIP question” is a difficult one to answer, because it’s possible that under their less popular leader this time around, many will just come home to the Conservatives regardless, and at the same time, you don’t want to alienate other factions of voters from places like Scotland and the Home Counties." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2574, "fields": { "answer": 5056, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "It’s always good to get across policy positions in interviews like this, but dear god did you come across as more wooden than a stool in this interview." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2587, "fields": { "answer": 5057, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "One part of this interview ended up becoming a bit of a meme, when you talked about your bookish upbringing, and your worst childhood mischief involving you running through fields of wheat. Jeremy Corbyn soon made a joke about your “terrible behaviour”" } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2588, "fields": { "answer": 5058, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "This probably wasn’t your best approach, as you just end up playing into Corbyn’s strategy with trying to redirect the conversation. Perhaps this is a gamble on that it’s already changed, and you’re adapting your campaign?" } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2589, "fields": { "answer": 5059, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Corbyn’s past is something that can certainly come back to haunt him. Bringing this up in the interview leads a lot of questions to come his way about if he would really disarm Britain’s nuclear weapons." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2590, "fields": { "answer": 5060, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "That’s probably the appropriate response. There’s no need to throw one side overboard unless you have to. However, the stability of this coalition might come into question." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2591, "fields": { "answer": 5061, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "You are leaning into the “hard Brexit” side of your supporters. With Brexit being as divisive an issue as it is, it’s unlikely that you’ll be able to hold up the coalition forever." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2592, "fields": { "answer": 5062, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "The “Norway Deal” is a soft Brexit position and will help you in Remain-voting regions like London and Scotland. You might risk neglecting Hard Brexit voters and struggle in the Red Wall however." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2593, "fields": { "answer": 5063, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "It’s difficult to say how effective this will be, if it will be palatable to both sides or just end up confusing your message. Generally though, ideas of border security are usually quite well received." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2594, "fields": { "answer": 5064, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Amber Rudd was the expected choice. It’s likely her expertise as Home Secretary will help in relation to issues involving national security." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2595, "fields": { "answer": 5065, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "David Davis wasn’t the expected choice, although sending him could be a good strategy when it comes to issues involving Brexit." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2596, "fields": { "answer": 5066, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Philip Hammond wasn’t the expected choice, but as he’s the Chancellor of the Exchequer, he will likely have an edge on economic policy in the debate." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2597, "fields": { "answer": 5067, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "This was very unexpected that you would turn up personally to the debate, but that ends up making it so all the main parties are present with their leaders." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2598, "fields": { "answer": 5068, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Amber Rudd throws some pot shots at the Liberal Democrats, but they mostly glance off. As the debate shifts away from Brexit towards domestic policies, Corbyn ends up winning strongly on policy after policy. A great night for Labour." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2599, "fields": { "answer": 5069, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Her attacks on UKIP don’t phase Paul Nuttall, but they probably don’t need to. This definitely curtails UKIP’s appeal with Brexit supporters who are uncomfortable with the far-right extremism that’s been exposed. As the debate shifts to domestic policy, Corbyn is the clear winner of the debate." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2600, "fields": { "answer": 5070, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "As the government, inevitably more attacks are going to come our way. If Rudd was really up to the challenge of defending from them, well… We’ll be honest, she didn’t do very well and started to break under the pressure. Corbyn won the debate by a country mile. " } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2601, "fields": { "answer": 5071, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "This would be the ideal approach, pick your target and stick to it, but the strategy falls apart when Tim Farron and Paul Nuttall end up taking turns to attack the Conservatives over Brexit, and Corbyn destroys them in the domestic portion. This will hurt us." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2602, "fields": { "answer": 5072, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Rallies aren’t polling stations, but they might signal something about the respective strength, or lack-of, in the support you have compared to Corbyn." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2603, "fields": { "answer": 5073, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "All in all, this might have been a decent decision. Whilst you have some awkward moments sometimes, it’s probably good that you’re getting out a bit more and talking to more people." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2605, "fields": { "answer": 5074, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "The larger rallies without too much prior planning go poorly, with you unable to generate the enthusiasm for the Conservative platform in the way Corbyn energises Labour supporters. Seeing the struggle, you reduce the size to smaller rallies with about 100 people. These go a little better." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2606, "fields": { "answer": 5075, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Perhaps that’s what it comes down to. Idealistic nonsense will get a crowd roaring, but you, Theresa May are the reality of the situation. People aren’t as enthusiastic about that, but perhaps on the big day people will come to their senses." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2607, "fields": { "answer": 5076, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Fully denying this is probably your safest option. The NHS is struggling, but you can’t be seen in any way convincing people of Corbyn’s accusations." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2608, "fields": { "answer": 5077, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Deny the accusations and shift the conversation as soon as possible to a weakness of your opponent. He ends up doing the same, bouncing it back to you. The issues of NHS funding and Trident end up growing with each iteration. Is someone hiding something here?" } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2609, "fields": { "answer": 5078, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "It may be your most realistic path, but it doesn’t inspire confidence in those concerned about the NHS. A slight vulnerability gets opened up aggressively as Corbyn continues to hammer his attacks about the Conservatives supposedly wanting to privatise the NHS." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2610, "fields": { "answer": 5079, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "Oh Theresa, what have you done? You’ve just given the game away haven’t you…" } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2611, "fields": { "answer": 5080, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "It’s probably best to move to a subject that’s more beneficial to you. Continuing to defend yourself from Corbyn’s attacks about the NHS just puts you in a position where you’re explaining, and therefore, losing." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2612, "fields": { "answer": 5081, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": " National security might be the greener pastures you need to move to. Or maybe not. Corbyn hits a strong attack against the Conservatives here as well, bringing up the austerity cuts removing 20,000 police officers from the streets." } }, { "model": "campaign_trail.answer_feedback", "pk": 2613, "fields": { "answer": 5387, "candidate": 200, "answer_feedback": "If you’re going to be able to sort this out, you need to make some concessions with these voters. Something has gone wrong if there’s that many people who want to vote for Tim Farron." } } ] campaignTrail_temp.jet_data = [{} ]
